<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U Xalatan Q1 sales $29 mln, Camptosar $41 mln.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U Xalatan Q1 sales $29 mln, Camptosar $41 mln.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. drugs group Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said on Wednesday sales of its anti-glaucoma agent Xalatan reached $29 million in the first quarter of 1997 while sales of cancer treatment Camptosar amounted to $41 million.  </p>
<p>Last year, Xalatan sold a total of $30 million, while sales of Camptosar were $59 million, Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said.</p>
<p>It did not break down the total on quarters although HSBC James Capel said in a March 6 research note that fourth quarter Xalatan sales amounted to $20 million and that Camptosar sales were $40 million in the same period.</p>
<p>-- Jorgen Osterberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
